{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289489-the-gender-pronoun-game-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate","id":1289489,"title":"The Gender Pronoun Game & Lunars: Fangs at the Gate","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-19T06:18:51-08:00","id":1289489,"title":"The Gender Pronoun Game & Lunars: Fangs at the Gate","content":"So I've been taking note of something in the manuscript and, incase the Topic title didn't give it away, it regards the usage of gender pronouns in the text and the arrangement of usage.<br /> <br /> So far we see a lot of You, They, It, She and Her, and not always in identifiable patterns. <br /> - Take for instance the text of the castes: Neutral, Neutral, Neutral, Femenine with an abrupt transition into Neutral again.<br /> - Merits are a mix of neutral and feminine<br /> - Charms are almost exclusively feminine except when referring to a resisting target, where it goes masculine.<br /> <br /> I noticed the same thing too in the dragon blooded books too but was surprised to see the same disparity here. This isn't even about the setting, or the NPCs, but directly speaking to the players themselves when explaining the rules.<br /> <br /> I'm all for equal representation, but shouldn't the assumption of the protagonists be kept more consistently neutral or try to keep the same ratios/parity with usages of such assumptions. E.G.:: Alternate by chapter, by charm tree or the like ? Keep it consistent within the same chapter or even the same paragraph/description (I'm looking at you Casteless !)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1759-kawaiiwolf","name":"kawaiiwolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1759_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T06:44:46-08:00","id":1289492,"title":"","content":"For charms, the intention of the writers is to use &quot;She&quot; for subject and &quot;He&quot; for object. This is useful, as English has no third-person pronouns that distinguish between subject and object (other than reflexive ones of course). If the book was in Arabic, obviously it wouldn't be necessary.<br /> <br /> They could say &quot;The Lunar&quot; and &quot;The Lunar's Target&quot;. But that uses more word count.<br /> <br /> <br /> For fluff about individuals, obviously they use a pronoun based on the individual's gender, which makes sense. Ma-Ha-Suchi is He, Rakshi is She, Silent Pearl is They, etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> Other than that, I haven't really noticed. Besides charm text (where it's important to be consistent), I don't care a huge deal. I guess &quot;They&quot; makes most sense when talking about a non-specific Lunar, but it's not very important.<br /> <br /> Whereas in the Dragonblood book, I think they were deliberately playing to the idea that the Realm is a sexist society where the assumption is that important people are female, and so speakers of High Realm or Low Realm will default to a female pronoun when discussing most roles.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, I see your point about consistency, but beyond the charmset and talking about specific individuals, I don't see it as a big issue. It's certainly not one that jumped out at me reading the book.*<br /> <br /> *Reading Dragonblood, the frequent use of female pronouns, even for non-specific Dragonblood, was very notable to me. Which is good, it should have been, because it really drove in the point that the Realm is a matriarchal society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-19-2019, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T06:52:25-08:00","id":1289496,"title":"","content":"Per the Onyx Path styleguide, we default to she/her in generic cases, with he/him being used if we need to distinguish. Any singular theys in there that aren't referring to a specifically nonbinary character are probably just me slipping up; that kind of stuff will get corrected in editing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":20}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T06:56:32-08:00","id":1289497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kawaiiwolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289489-the-gender-pronoun-game-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate#post1289489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take for instance the text of the castes: Neutral, Neutral, Neutral, Femenine with an abrupt transition into Neutral again.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's actually plural, plural, plural, one sentence in the singular, with the rest of the Casteless spread in the plural.<br /> <br /> The Merits and Charms consistently refer to the character as <i>she</i> and her target as <i>he</i>.<br /> <br /> The chargen chapter addresses the player directly, and so uses <i>you</i>.<br /> <br /> It's pretty consistent, all in all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T07:01:24-08:00","id":1289499,"title":"","content":"Damnit English!<br /> <br /> Why can't you distinguish between third-person-plural and unknown-gender-third-person-singular! Mandarin does it, why can't English? (Although I guess Mandarin's third-person-plural has issues of clarity in other ways.)<br /> <br /> Still, it's not as bad as British English's failure to distinguish between second-person-plural and second-person-singular, which frankly is embarressing. Texans can manage it, why can't we?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T07:24:11-08:00","id":1289517,"title":"","content":"English is three different languages standing on each other's shoulders under a trenchcoat, trying to pass themselves off as a single, legitimate language. It is a mongrel language that not only requires children take vocabulary lessons, but spelling lessons, because it follows at least three different spelling conventions.<br /> <br /> Making this misbegotten tongue the new Lingua Franca of the world is but one of the British Empire's many sins.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, certainly one of the reasons why feminine pronouns are used as the subject and male pronouns are used as the object is because of the gendered double-standard that makes it more acceptable for a male to be the target of deliberate action by a female than the reverse, especially in a context where most of the language concerns attacking with intent to kill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T07:39:12-08:00","id":1289523,"title":"","content":"Or, you know, because female for subject has been industry standard since the 90\u2019s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T07:54:38-08:00","id":1289528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289489-the-gender-pronoun-game-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1289523#post1289523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, you know, because female for subject has been industry standard since the 90\u2019s.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh.<br /> <br /> That is... emphatically not the case.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T08:39:26-08:00","id":1289541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289489-the-gender-pronoun-game-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1289523#post1289523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, you know, because female for subject has been industry standard since the 90\u2019s.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really only for WW, and I think Exalted 3e has actually been one of the most sytmeatic of it even then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T08:52:30-08:00","id":1289543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kawaiiwolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289489-the-gender-pronoun-game-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate#post1289489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm all for equal representation, but shouldn't the assumption of the protagonists be kept more consistently neutral or try to keep the same ratios/parity with usages of such assumptions. E.G.:: Alternate by chapter, by charm tree or the like ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh god, that would be hell.<br /> <br /> Gender politics aside, I think that OP's style guide makes the text of charms very clear. The She/He distinction makes it very obvious who the actor and the target are without tortured constructions like &quot;The lunar activating this charm,&quot; &quot;This charm's target,&quot; etc. Alternating by charm tree would be incredibly confusing, which is reason enough not to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10995-abakus","name":"Abakus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T09:07:01-08:00","id":1289552,"title":"","content":"Kind of an example of the opposite to me was reading Scion, where it very often alternated. And this did a lot to mess with clarity after how much I got use to Exalted's use of pronouns as actual tools of language. Despite some areas of roughness in the Charmset design, that's one thing I am fully behind now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T09:32:07-08:00","id":1289561,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#DDA0DD\">I'm calling male genocide.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T09:44:28-08:00","id":1289565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289489-the-gender-pronoun-game-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1289517#post1289517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">English is three different languages standing on each other's shoulders under a trenchcoat, trying to pass themselves off as a single, legitimate language.</div> </div> </div> </div>Three?<br /> There's a lot more than three.<br /> <br /> I mean, obviously it's primarily a West Germanic grammar-base with Norman vocabulary, but it has bits of Celtic, Latin and Norman grammar. Then the vocabulary has Germanic base words, Norman, Old French, Latin and Greek vocabulary, plus a bit of Norse, and then obviously loanwords from everywhere.<br /> <br /> Still, loan-words aren't exactly uncommon in other languages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is a mongrel language that not only requires children take vocabulary lessons, </div> </div> </div>Most languages do that. Admittedly, English is worse, because it has probably the world's largest lexical corpus. But then, that's an advantage for specificity and poetry. And it makes it useful as a technical language.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> spelling lessons, because it follows at least three different spelling conventions. </div> </div> </div>Again, any language with a writing lesson requires spelling (or equivalent) lessons.<br /> <br /> But certainly Italian, Korean, etc, have much easier spelling.<br /> <br /> Still, it could be worse. It's way easier than Chinese. I'll also say that European and Asian students' English spelling is shockingly good; spelling isn't a huge issue for them.<br /> (Unlike Arabs and Persians.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Making this misbegotten tongue the new Lingua Franca of the world is but one of the British Empire's many sins. </div> </div> </div>It's useful as a technical language because of its huge corpus, and obviously users of technical language need a Lingua Franca more than users of<br /> <br /> There's also some research that says the stress patterns and the vague-but-not-exact spelling-sound link is actually easier for L2 users to pick up than a fully-phonetic alphabet (like Italian). I haven't read it myself though, so I don't know how true that is. It sounds a bit dubious to me, but obviously having a phonetic alphabet for a Lingua Franca is essentially impossible.<br /> <br /> Still, you could do better than English does.<br /> <br /> <br /> Obviously there's also the fact that it's an Indo-European language (the most widespread language family), that it uses an alphabet (much harder for the barely literature than characters, but much better for the fully literate), that the wide range of loan words means most L2 users will find something they know, etc.<br /> Essentially, a Lingua Franca works much better if it's a mash-up of several foreign languages than if it's a Language Isolate. Can you imagine how difficult it would be if Basque was the Lingua Franca?<br /> Whereas for North Europeans English is pretty easy (my school has recently given up teaching Danish high-school students General English; they're just too good), and for Southern Europeans it's not very difficult.<br /> <br /> Were I to pick a language to be a Lingua Franca, I'm not sure English would be no.1, but it'd be in the top 5.<br /> <br /> (Obviously there's way better <i>hypothetical </i>languages, but I'm talking about real languages.)<br /> <br /> I assume Chomsky would argue that the easiest Lingua France would be Interlanguage, but Interlanguage is a bit rubbish.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, certainly one of the reasons why feminine pronouns are used as the subject and male pronouns are used as the object is because of the gendered double-standard that makes it more acceptable for a male to be the target of deliberate action by a female than the reverse, especially in a context where most of the language concerns attacking with intent to kill. </div> </div> </div>I see your point, but I doubt that was a deliberate intention.<br /> <br /> I suspect the intention of trying to use female pronouns as the subject was simply to make roleplaying games more attractive to women. 80s roleplaying games didn't exactly consider women a significant target audience.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T10:10:51-08:00","id":1289575,"title":"","content":"I like to think of it from an in-setting point of view. Many eras, certainly most on a years-based count, of the Ages of Man were heavily influenced by top political positions being long-held by women (Scarlet Empress, Merela, to name but two). So the default actor is a she. I've observed the convention in my own homebrew/fanfiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T11:00:19-08:00","id":1289588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289489-the-gender-pronoun-game-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1289496#post1289496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Per the Onyx Path styleguide, we default to she/her in generic cases, with he/him being used if we need to distinguish. Any singular theys in there that aren't referring to a specifically nonbinary character are probably just me slipping up; that kind of stuff will get corrected in editing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. Did this get changed when Onyxpath became its own entity different from the old Whitewolf. Didn\u2019t say for instance the old Whitewolf guidelines basically just shift gender references each time so they had half and half usage in Examples? This newer Guideline does make sense for clarity and order reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T11:15:26-08:00","id":1289593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289489-the-gender-pronoun-game-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1289499#post1289499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damnit English!<br /> <br /> Why can't you distinguish between third-person-plural and unknown-gender-third-person-singular! Mandarin does it, why can't English? (Although I guess Mandarin's third-person-plural has issues of clarity in other ways.)<br /> <br /> Still, it's not as bad as British English's failure to distinguish between second-person-plural and second-person-singular, which frankly is embarressing. Texans can manage it, why can't we?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, British people can't tell the difference between you singular and you plural based on context?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T11:27:54-08:00","id":1289597,"title":"","content":"Generally yes. That's why we haven't bothered to develop a plural version of you.<br /> <br /> But it's not 100%. Contextual language rarely is.<br /> <br /> Hence the useful term &quot;Y'all&quot;. But we don't have an equivalent.<br /> <br /> Personally, I use &quot;You guys&quot; when referring to a group (which is also an Americanism) but it's unfortunately gendered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-19-2019, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T11:51:25-08:00","id":1289604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289489-the-gender-pronoun-game-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1289597#post1289597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hence the useful term &quot;Y'all&quot;. But we don't have an equivalent.<br /> <br /> Personally, I use &quot;You guys&quot; when referring to a group (which is also an Americanism) but it's unfortunately gendered.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth, as a Midwesterner, &quot;you guys&quot; as a plural is largely, effectively de-gendered. In Chicago, at least, &quot;guys&quot; can be gendered or not, based on context. &quot;Going out with the guys&quot; is gendered, while using &quot;you guys&quot; or greeting a group of people as &quot;Hey guys&quot; is more or less gender-neutral. <br /> <br /> That said, I spent my university years in Texas, and I will spend the rest of my life saying &quot;y'all.&quot; The word is so convenient, it's downright insidious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10995-abakus","name":"Abakus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T12:37:31-08:00","id":1289612,"title":"","content":"Y'all has become singular in some places from overuse leading to the double plural construction all y'all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T14:28:06-08:00","id":1289653,"title":"","content":"I'm from Ontario and I use y'all all the time. It's just helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T14:41:20-08:00","id":1289654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289489-the-gender-pronoun-game-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1289593#post1289593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, British people can't tell the difference between you singular and you plural based on context?</div> </div> </div> </div>*rit en Fran\u00e7ais*<br /> <br /> *would laugh harder in Dutch, but sucks too much at it for that*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T15:03:28-08:00","id":1289660,"title":"","content":"The only reason not to use &quot;y'all&quot; is contempt for the low-born commoners who grow your food.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T15:20:23-08:00","id":1289665,"title":"","content":"While we\u2019re discussing pronoun limitation- it would also be nice if we could distinguish inclusive vs exclusive first person plural (i.e. does \u201cwe\u201d/\u201cus\u201d include the person being addressed or not). Like whether \u201cyou\u201d is plural or not, it is sometimes clear from context, but not always.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T15:25:24-08:00","id":1289668,"title":"","content":"I don't mind the current style guide too much. &quot;They&quot; is a plural and not a singular, but it's a lot better than the x* pronoun set or whatever other linguistic fashion comes and goes. <br /> <br /> I suppose when you get right down to it, I'd rather a fantasy game's prose avoid placing itself in a particular real-world time, culture, and current-events topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T15:42:22-08:00","id":1289676,"title":"","content":"&quot;I saw someone in the distance, but I couldn't tell who they were.&quot;<br /> &quot;Someone called me, but they didn't leave a message.&quot;<br /> &quot;Who was the person who helped you? We should thank them.&quot;<br /> &quot;I have an appointment on Wednesday with a doctor, but I don't know their name.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;They&quot; can be singular. We use it to refer to someone whose gender is unknown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T15:43:53-08:00","id":1289680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289489-the-gender-pronoun-game-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1289668#post1289668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mind the current style guide too much. &quot;They&quot; is a plural and not a singular, but it's a lot better than the x* pronoun set or whatever other linguistic fashion comes and goes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Singular they has been part of English for 400 years. Shakespeare used it. Jane Austen used it. People who complain about other people using it use it all the time without thinking. It has always been part of Modern English from any remotely descriptivist analysis.<br /> <br /> Edit: This is the SAT question that made me quit tutoring in a rage <img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/ry7mZBm/11224047-10100557439508684-6845761410518807344-n.jpg \" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 02-19-2019, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T16:14:53-08:00","id":1289690,"title":"","content":"Indeed, and I can accept that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The usage gets tied in a knot sometimes though. &quot;They use their power to uplift their Chosen.&quot; reads as a different meaning than &quot;She uses her power to uplift her Chosen.&quot; for instance.<br /> <br /> Not sure if there's a particular way out of that. I appreciate the topic and effort in any case.<br /> <br /> <br /> [Edit to add: I award you a Linguistics specialty for taking on that SAT question!]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":6192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","user":"Simon Darkstep","date":". 02-19-2019, 07:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T16:31:29-08:00","id":1289696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289489-the-gender-pronoun-game-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1289690#post1289690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> [Edit to add: I award you a Linguistics specialty for taking on that SAT question!]</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> For what it's worth the INTENDED answer is &quot;D&quot;, the ACTUALLY CORRECT answer is &quot;E&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T16:37:01-08:00","id":1289697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289489-the-gender-pronoun-game-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1289696#post1289696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> For what it's worth the INTENDED answer is &quot;D&quot;, the ACTUALLY CORRECT answer is &quot;E&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> .... there was a question? <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T18:20:11-08:00","id":1289728,"title":"","content":"&quot;Pineapples don't have sleeves.&quot;<br /> <br /> I fucking hate standardized tests.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T19:52:28-08:00","id":1289765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289489-the-gender-pronoun-game-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1289676#post1289676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I saw someone in the distance, but I couldn't tell who they were.&quot;<br /> &quot;Someone called me, but they didn't leave a message.&quot;<br /> &quot;Who was the person who helped you? We should thank them.&quot;<br /> &quot;I have an appointment on Wednesday with a doctor, but I don't know their name.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;They&quot; can be singular. We use it to refer to someone whose gender is unknown.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the problem is when it becomes or remains unclear whether you are referring to a singular individual or a group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T20:17:26-08:00","id":1289771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289489-the-gender-pronoun-game-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1289496#post1289496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Per the Onyx Path styleguide, we default to she/her in generic cases, with he/him being used if we need to distinguish. Any singular theys in there that aren't referring to a specifically nonbinary character are probably just me slipping up; that kind of stuff will get corrected in editing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the clarification !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1759-kawaiiwolf","name":"kawaiiwolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1759_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T21:00:46-08:00","id":1289786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289489-the-gender-pronoun-game-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1289597#post1289597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally yes. That's why we haven't bothered to develop a plural version of you.<br /> <br /> But it's not 100%. Contextual language rarely is.<br /> <br /> Hence the useful term &quot;Y'all&quot;. But we don't have an equivalent.<br /> <br /> Personally, I use &quot;You guys&quot; when referring to a group (which is also an Americanism) but it's unfortunately gendered.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, okay, you meant you don't have a word that makes it automatically clear free of context. That makes more sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T08:26:48-08:00","id":1289938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289489-the-gender-pronoun-game-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1289696#post1289696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> For what it's worth the INTENDED answer is &quot;D&quot;, the ACTUALLY CORRECT answer is &quot;E&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why is E correct? Each is singular. A lot fo people don't USE it that way, so colloquially either is fine, sure, but as far as formal rules go, D is wrong. It should be &quot;its.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10995-abakus","name":"Abakus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T08:31:54-08:00","id":1289940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Abakus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289489-the-gender-pronoun-game-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1289938#post1289938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Why is E correct? Each is singular. A lot fo people don't USE it that way, so colloquially either is fine, sure, but as far as formal rules go, D is wrong. It should be &quot;its.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course \u201ceach\u201d is singular. So is gender-ambiguous singular \u201ctheir\u201d. You NEVER use \u201cit/its\u201d for a person. People who are wrong think that the \u201ctheir\u201d should be \u201chis or her\u201d - but they are incorrect as gender-ambiguous singular \u201cthey/their\u201d has been correct mainstream English for 400 years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T08:34:50-08:00","id":1289941,"title":"","content":"I don't even know what you're supposed to do there. Find the errors? The error is E, because that's not even a sentence.<br /> D is fine. The players (plural) are practicing their plays.<br /> Unless it means the players are practicing its (the team's) plays.<br /> <br /> I have no idea how Americans talk about sports. Do you refer to individual plays, or the overall team's plays? (We wouldn't even call them plays, probably.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T13:26:20-08:00","id":1290080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289489-the-gender-pronoun-game-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1289940#post1289940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course \u201ceach\u201d is singular. So is gender-ambiguous singular \u201ctheir\u201d. You NEVER use \u201cit/its\u201d for a person. People who are wrong think that the \u201ctheir\u201d should be \u201chis or her\u201d - but they are incorrect as gender-ambiguous singular \u201cthey/their\u201d has been correct mainstream English for 400 years.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> AH, I see. I had dropped a word reading the example (&quot;each of the teams&quot; rather than &quot;each of the team members&quot;). Teaches me to do proofreading before I've had coffee!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10995-abakus","name":"Abakus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T19:34:00-08:00","id":1290210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289489-the-gender-pronoun-game-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1289941#post1289941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't even know what you're supposed to do there. Find the errors?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that instruction is at the beginning of the section, and I just snapped a photo of the question in my rage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T07:58:17-08:00","id":1290347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289489-the-gender-pronoun-game-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1289541#post1289541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really only for WW, and I think Exalted 3e has actually been one of the most sytmeatic of it even then.</div> </div> </div> </div>And there's a likely reason for that. In most saxon and latin languages the male pronouns tend to absorb the neutrals and especially the mixed subjects. So defaulting to she is an inversion of how most of this half of the world is used to process language.<br /> <br /> It's minor, at least. Most people just run over it and read the other way around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 02-21-2019, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T10:31:24-08:00","id":1290423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289489-the-gender-pronoun-game-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1290347#post1290347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And there's a likely reason for that. In most saxon and latin languages the male pronouns tend to absorb the neutrals and especially the mixed subjects. So defaulting to she is an inversion of how most of this half of the world is used to process language.<br /> <br /> It's minor, at least. Most people just run over it and read the other way around.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's actually even worse when one reads the history of it. Neutral singular they has been a part of English for a while, and wasn't pushed out for default &quot;he&quot; until the mid-19th Century.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Singular_they#Prescription_of_generic_he\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/My_pronoun_is_THEY_-_International_Design_in_Government_Day_at_Code_for_America_Summit_2019_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-My_pronoun_is_THEY_-_International_Design_in_Government_Day_at_Code_for_America_Summit_2019_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Singular_they#Prescription_of_generic_he\" target=\"_blank\"> Singular they - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Singular_they#Prescription_of_generic_he\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Singular_they#Prescription_of_generic_he </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Good ol' prescriptivist grammar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T11:02:06-08:00","id":1290433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289489-the-gender-pronoun-game-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1290423#post1290423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's actually even worse when one reads the history of it. Neutral singular they has been a part of English for a while, and wasn't pushed out for default &quot;he&quot; until the mid-19th Century.<br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Singular_they#Prescription_of_generic_he\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Singul..._of_generic_he</a><br /> <br /> Good ol' prescriptivist grammar.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of cultural assumptions about the past are myths invented specifically by Victorians in their epic quest to ruin literally everything.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a ton of evidence for example that women owned and run businesses, either on their own or as equal partners with their husbands, were common place before the 19th century, and the rise of moralist crusades to \u201cprotect\u201d the \u201cangels of the home\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 02-21-2019, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T11:13:59-08:00","id":1290440,"title":"","content":"It's really, REALLY hard to peg these changes as active efforts made by anyone. That's just not how languages evolve, because no one owns language.<br /> English's case is most likely a simplification from its saxon roots, as german did and still does have neutral pronouns.<br /> <br /> Time to seek the pros.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T11:24:04-08:00","id":1290443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289489-the-gender-pronoun-game-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1290440#post1290440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's really, REALLY hard to peg these changes as active efforts made by anyone. That's just not how languages evolve, because no one owns language.<br /> English's case is most likely a simplification from its saxon roots, as german did and still does have neutral pronouns.<br /> <br /> Time to seek the pros.</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of the actual evolution of language as it\u2019s used, yes, agreed.<br /> <br /> In terms of prescriptivist positions completely out of step with how the language is actually used, like \u201cgender-ambiguous singular they is incorrect, \u2018they\u2019 can only be plural\u201d - those can be nailed down pretty readily as the work of specific people, or at least a small elite class.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 02-21-2019, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T19:42:56-08:00","id":1290636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289489-the-gender-pronoun-game-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1290440#post1290440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's really, REALLY hard to peg these changes as active efforts made by anyone. That's just not how languages evolve, because no one owns language.<br /> English's case is most likely a simplification from its saxon roots, as german did and still does have neutral pronouns.<br /> <br /> Time to seek the pros.</div> </div> </div> </div>English is kind of weird in this. While there is natural language progression, states and marekts have had effects on things. While English doens't have an Academy like other European languages, there has been a healthy market of grammar books and academic writing which has had some influnce on the use of pronouns in well, prescribed writing.<br /> <br /> Default &quot;he&quot; mostly being imposed had that happen. English and American style guides became immportant to how English was written to broad masses, and that in turn would have affected a lot of the natural envolution of htings. English it's less this whole deep history of pronouns, and more the way purposeful decisions and market forces played out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T20:03:33-08:00","id":1290641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289489-the-gender-pronoun-game-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1290636#post1290636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">English is kind of weird in this. While there is natural language progression, states and marekts have had effects on things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell, <i>The Flintstones</i> managed to wreak at least one notable change in the language, back when they were hocking cigarettes!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T09:48:02-08:00","id":1290806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289489-the-gender-pronoun-game-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1290641#post1290641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, <i>The Flintstones</i> managed to wreak at least one notable change in the language, back when they were hocking cigarettes!</div> </div> </div> </div>Which change is that?<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: The reason \u201cnimrod\u201d is used to mean \u201cidiot\u201d is because a generation of kids weren\u2019t familiar with the sarcastic allusion that Bugs Bunny was making to a mighty Biblical hunter. He was calling Elmer Fudd \u201cNimrod\u201d the way someone might sarcastically use \u201cEinstein\u201d - but kids who didn\u2019t know who Nimrod was could tell by context it was an insult and just picked it up as meaning \u201cdumb\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 02-22-2019, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T10:11:43-08:00","id":1290817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289489-the-gender-pronoun-game-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1289765#post1289765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the problem is when it becomes or remains unclear whether you are referring to a singular individual or a group.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but that's the same with You.<br /> <br /> All of the examples I gave clearly state they are singular, by use of singular countable nouns or pronouns (person, someone, etc).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T11:18:44-08:00","id":1290840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289489-the-gender-pronoun-game-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1290817#post1290817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but that's the same with You.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a problem for those who don't appreciate the beauty of &quot;Y'all&quot;. Or &quot;you all&quot;.<br /> <br /> Which reminds me that Southerns also have a partial solution to third person pronouns with &quot;them all&quot; and &quot;all of them&quot;. We just need to take the bold step into coining the term &quot;th'all&quot;.<br /> <br /> Third person plural possessive would be &quot;th'all's&quot;, just as second personal plural possessive is &quot;y'all's&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T14:11:40-08:00","id":1290903,"title":"","content":"Well, that's what I was saying earlier. Seems sensible to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T15:08:20-08:00","id":1290914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289489-the-gender-pronoun-game-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1290806#post1290806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which change is that?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winston_tastes_good_like_a_cigarette_should#Grammar_controversy\" target=\"_blank\">Folks considered using &quot;like&quot; as a conjunction to be &quot;ungrammatical and provocative.&quot;</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-22-2019, 06:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T15:56:38-08:00","id":1290921,"title":"","content":"I suppose it's only fitting that, after ten or more years of an endless multitude of threads transforming at the merest mention of Lunars, that the introduction of Lunars at the height of their powers be commemorated by a thread that starts off nominally about them, and then immediately transforms into a general discussion of grammatical and etymological intricacies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T16:56:21-08:00","id":1290930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289489-the-gender-pronoun-game-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1290921#post1290921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose it's only fitting that, after ten or more years of an endless multitude of threads transforming at the merest mention of Lunars, that the introduction of Lunars at the height of their powers be commemorated by a thread that starts off nominally about them, and then immediately transforms into a general discussion of grammatical and etymological intricacies.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's-... It's like the inverse of Meerkat Steals the Spotlight Prana. It's kind of beautiful, actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T20:29:35-08:00","id":1290984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289489-the-gender-pronoun-game-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1290921#post1290921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose it's only fitting that, after ten or more years of an endless multitude of threads transforming at the merest mention of Lunars, that the introduction of Lunars at the height of their powers be commemorated by a thread that starts off nominally about them, and then immediately transforms into a general discussion of grammatical and etymological intricacies.</div> </div> </div> </div>As the person perhaps most responsible for that phenomenon (or at least the only such person I know about who still posts in the official forums), this is not the first time. Granted, it is rare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T01:11:28-08:00","id":1291036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289489-the-gender-pronoun-game-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1289499#post1289499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, it's not as bad as British English's failure to distinguish between second-person-plural and second-person-singular, which frankly is embarressing. Texans can manage it, why can't we?</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that's not really the case.<br /> <br /> Northern dialects of British English (and Scots English) do have a plural form of you: yous or youse. You'll also see 'you lot' or 'yous lot' across Britain, or 'yas' (as in plural of 'ya', not 'yaaaasss queen').<br /> <br /> Then there's the archaic (but surprisingly durable) 'ye' (again, especially in the North of England and Scotland, but also in Ireland): <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ye_(pronoun\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ye_(pronoun</a>)<br /> <br /> I've also seen and heard 'yeez', which is probably from ye.<br /> <br /> See here: <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/You#Informal_plural_forms\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/You#...l_plural_forms</a><br /> <br /> Yes, these are informal, but so is the Texan 'y'all'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 02-23-2019, 04:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T05:33:53-08:00","id":1291504,"title":"","content":"Since we're talking of informal pronouns, I have to mention youns. We say that one in tennessee. <br /> <br /> What's weird is some people here are slightly racist(statesist?) about it too. If you say youns you're from tennessee and therefore cool. If you ya'll then at least you're a southerner. Except some people born in tennessee still say ya'll so it's actually a complete and utter fail on the people that think that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20546-dragonchild","name":"Dragonchild","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T17:39:56-07:00","id":1295699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonchild</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289489-the-gender-pronoun-game-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1291504#post1291504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since we're talking of informal pronouns, I have to mention youns. We say that one in tennessee. <br /> <br /> What's weird is some people here are slightly racist(statesist?) about it too. If you say youns you're from tennessee and therefore cool. If you ya'll then at least you're a southerner. Except some people born in tennessee still say ya'll so it's actually a complete and utter fail on the people that think that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's only that way because Tennessee is actually three states split more or less equally along its width that each have their own culture. People from Memphis speak and sound nothing like people from Chattanooga and kids come back from Knoxville with weird vocabulary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],